{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791661998,"nonce":"ik68XxvEVYcsNX1daTXZ/oFFzNg=","title":"Containers: schema version guard and backup before migrate","message":"Spec 018 rev 2 section Version skew (ticket C12). Must land before C4. The host checkout and the image share one database, and db.migrate applies missing migrations on any command and at console start. (1) connect/migrate refuses when schema_version holds a version this code does not know, with the message database is newer than this jobhunter (code has N, database has M), and the console shows it instead of starting; (2) before applying any pending migration, take an automatic backup through the online backup API into \u003cdata_dir\u003e/backups/auto/pre-migrate-\u003cfrom\u003e-\u003cto\u003e-\u003cUTC\u003eZ.db (C6 naming); (3) jobhunter version prints package version, git commit if known, and the highest migration number; the image records the commit as an OCI label and env JOBHUNTER_BUILD_COMMIT. Checks without podman: pytest on a tmp DB with an extra fake schema_version row (refuses, nothing written), pending-migration test that the backup exists and passes integrity_check before the first migration runs; ruff and pytest. Needs the user on the host: run jobhunter version on host and in the image and compare.","files":null}]}